From 138346a06bb0d0c3abd8902cbe27f0f0f8da92a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TRM <trm@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:00:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Instella MoE: gated attention + FarSkip two-stream residual

InstellaMoEForCausalLM is DeepSeek-V3 plus two ops this graph lacked; both now live in the
deepseek2 arch behind optional GGUF keys that default to off, so existing DeepSeek GGUFs are
byte-for-byte unchanged in behaviour.

  MLAGatedAttention: attn_output *= sigmoid(attn_gate @ normed_input) BEFORE o_proj
    (build_attn called with wo=nullptr, gate, then build_lora_mm(wo))
  FarSkip-Collective: two residual streams - r = h_full + attn(read from h_norouted);
    h_norouted = r + shared; h_full = r + routed + shared. A dense layer emits one stream
    (HF returns a tensor not a tuple) so the second stream starts at the first MoE layer.

keys: deepseek2.gated_attention / far_skip / far_skip_start_idx / far_skip_end_idx
converter: conversion/instella.py (fails closed on attn_only_farskip, mlp_only_farskip)
doc: docs/instella-farskip.md

Verified on F:/models/instella-moe-think -> 457-tensor 16.9 GB q8_0 GGUF with
gated_attention=1 far_skip=1 start=0 end=26; loads and generates coherent text.
